" (leadership may imply cooperation but not explicit). Also \"can anticipate dangerous situations\", \"can see complex connections\", \"excellent spatial vision\". Also \"sometimes not good at taking criticism\", \"can be unorganized\". No explicit crew cooperation note.\n\nCandidate B: \"can be uncooperative\" (explicit). Also \"very conscientious\", \"handles stress well\", \"good at assessing weather\", \"excellent computer skills\". Also \"can be grumpy\". So crew cooperation: uncooperative, grumpy.\n\nCandidate C: \"creates a positive atmosphere with his crew\" (explicit positive crew cooperation). Also \"regarded as egocentric\", \"difficulty communicating ideas\". But positive atmosphere suggests good cooperation.\n\nCandidate D: \"regarded as arrogant\", \"relatively weak leadership skills\". Also \"loner\"? Actually note: \"D is regarded as arrogant.\" Also \"D is considered a loner\"? The note says \"D is regarded as arrogant.\" Also \"D is considered a loner\"? The note: \"D is regarded as arrogant.\" Also \"D is considered a loner\"? The note: \"D is regarded as arrogant.\" Also \"D is considered a loner\"? The note: \"D is regarded as arrogant.\" Also \"D is considered a loner.\" Actually the note: \"D is regarded as arrogant.\" and earlier \"D is considered a loner.\" Yes: \"D is regarded as arrogant.\" and \"D is considered a loner.\" So crew cooperation: likely poor.\n\nThus answer: A: no explicit observation on crew cooperation. B: uncooperative, grumpy. C: creates positive atmosphere with crew. D: regarded as arrogant, considered a loner (implies poor cooperation). Provide that.\n\nWe must not add extra. Provide answer only."}
